    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on the new affordable housing mandate for the district. We have a set number of units coming online and need to decide how to actually dole them out. People are arguing about lotteries vs income-based vs transit-proximate. In your professional opinion, what is the most equitable way to distribute these units?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A mixed approach combining a lottery for unmet transparency with strict income-based criteria for affordability is generally considered the most equitable method. This ensures fair access for those with a higher need while preventing speculative hoarding of units. You might also prioritize a small subset of applicants based on transit proximity to further support essential workers. The key is to clearly define and publicly share the weight of each factor in your decision process to build community trust.",
