      "content": "A pure lottery ignores critical need, often allowing those with the most financial capacity to \"win\" without a “needy” home to afford it. In a mixed model, income-based eligibility directly prioritizes vulnerable populations who lack other land tenure options, while the lottery component ensures fairness among those strictly meeting affordability standards. This targeted approach is more equitable because it aligns resource distribution with actual housing security goals rather than treating all applicants as equal. Ultimately, equity depends on defining \"fairness\" as providing shelter to the most in need first rather than lottery randomness.",
